  "id": "COMPOUND:28794 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Michaolide J and HuT78 through a series of molecular targets. Michaolide J is implicated in targeting Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is a key protein involved in cellular redox regulation and oxidative stress response. This target is also engaged by multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, Uvaol-3-Caffeate, and Phorone, all of which have been shown to interact with HuT78. These compounds likely exert their effects through shared mechanisms, possibly by modulating the same biological pathways or by acting as ligands for similar molecular targets. The consistent targeting of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial across these compounds implies a common functional role in cellular processes, which may explain the observed interaction with HuT78. The evidence supports a pathway where Michaolide J may act as a modulator of Thioredoxin, thereby influencing HuT78's function through this shared target.",
